We also see that $(x,y)$ lies on the boundary line of the blue-dashed line $2x+y=2$, so we substitute $y=2-2x$ into the equation of $y=x$ to get $y=x=2-2x\Rightarrow x=\frac{2}{3}$. Therefore, we can compute that  $(x,y)=\left(\frac{2}{3},\frac{2}{3}\right)$.

