We can reduce the argument since the tangent function has period $360^\circ$: \begin{align*}
\tan(-3645^\circ) &= \tan(-3645^\circ + 10 \cdot 360^\circ)\\
&= \tan(-45^\circ)\\
&= \boxed{-1}.
\end{align*}
