Case 2: $x < 0.$

Then $2^{-x} + 3(-x) = 18.$  Let $y = |x|.$  Then this equation becomes $2^y - 3y = 18.$  It is easy to check that $y = 3,$ which means $|x| = 3,$ which means $x = -3.$

The sum of the solutions is therefore $-3 + 3 = \boxed{0}.$
