Let this circle have radius $R.$  Then by law of cosines,
\[\angle BPP' = \angle BPA' = \arcsin \left( \frac{BP' \cdot PP'}{AP' \cdot AB} \right) = \arcsin \left( \frac{AP}{AB} \right) = \arccos \left( \cos \widehat{APC} \right) = \arccos \frac{4}{5}.\]Then
\[\angle BPC = \frac{\widehat{BP} + \widehat{CP}}{2} = \arccos \frac{4}{5}.\]Then $\cos \angle BPC = \cos (2 \angle BPC/2) = 1 - 2 \sin^2 \angle BPC,$ so
\[2 \sin^2 \angle BPC = 1 - \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^2 = \frac{9}{25}.\]Thus, $\sin (2 \angle BPC) = \frac{2 \cdot 9}{25} = \boxed{\frac{18}{25}}.$
